WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.720
What is the best moment in all of One Piece?

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.290
Is it Robin’s desperate, I want to Live?

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:10.810
And does that moment rank above or below when
Luffy absolutely destroyed this celestial

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.810
dragon?

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:17.279
Or could both of those even fall behind this
island-shaking clash between Whitebeard and

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:18.279
Roger?

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:23.070
Let’s find out as I take on the impossible
challenge of ranking the twenty-three best

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.830
moments in all of One Piece

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.850
Starting with a moment that literally saved
Sanji’s life.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:32.840
In chapter 58, Sanji and his mentor Zeff were
stranded on this deserted island.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.890
Now, at this time the young cook hates this
old man because Zeff’s crew basically killed

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.690
Snaji’s former crewmates.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:44.180
Seventy days later Sanji is starving and about
to die, so he plans to steal Zeff’s remaining

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.180
food.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.960
However, he quickly learns that all Zeff has
is treasure, and then he is stunned when he

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.500
sees THIS.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:58.140
This brutal scene makes Sanji cry like a little
baby, and he realizes that Zeff literally

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:04.330
cut off AND ate his own leg JUST so Sanji
would have more food to eat.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:09.500
And while this might be an unexpected moment
to make this list, just wait until you see

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.700
which shocking moment I ranked inside my top
three.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:18.000
However, a character eating their own leg
is just the tip of the iceberg when it comes

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.930
to the Straw Hat’s heart-breaking backstories.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:23.890
And that is absolutely true for Brook’s
flashback.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:29.990
Which - let me tell you -&nbsp; this moment absolutely
ruined me.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:36.361
His crew is dying from a deadly disease, and
the music loving crew join together in one

00:01:36.361 --> 00:01:38.460
last tear-jerking encore.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:44.590
And as Brook’s crewmates dropped one by
one, I was literally crying my eyes out.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.000
What a moment of utter sadness.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.149
What’s crazy about this story though is
that it can make you feel pure sadness but

00:01:54.149 --> 00:01:55.770
also absolute joy.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:02.119
And no scene captures the joy of the story
as much as this epic panel right here.

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:03.119
Just looking at it makes me smile.

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:06.430
That’s because we’ve just witnessed the
former pirate king’s epic journey to reach

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.799
the end of the Grand Line.

00:02:07.799 --> 00:02:12.660
And as we are all on the edge of our seats
wondering if we will see what the One Piece

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.900
treasure actually is, we only get to see their
legendary reaction.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.580
Everyone laughs.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:27.080
But not just any laugh, a true feeling of
absolute joy.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.670
Which only makes me even more curious about
what this treasure really is.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.900
And if this moment is only at number 21, just
wait until you see what is coming next…

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.640
Because here we have one of the most jaw dropping
moments in the story.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:47.080
Luffy has battled his way through HUNDREDS
of enemies on Enies Lobby as he tries to rescue

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.080
Robin.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:53.000
And everything was going smoothly until he
was stopped by this guy.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:03:00.769
And this government secret agent was basically
UNTOUCHABLE at this point until Luffy revealed

00:03:00.769 --> 00:03:01.769
this.

00:03:01.769 --> 00:03:04.299
Wow, this absolutely blew my mind.

00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:10.099
For the first time in the story, Luffy showed
an actual power up, and he immediately demolished

00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:14.510
the government agent with his new super-charged
speed and strength.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:19.470
While this was an incredibly hyped moment
in Luffy’s journey, perhaps no event was

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.409
more important to him than the next one.

00:03:22.409 --> 00:03:27.269
That’s because all the way back in chapter
one, Shanks gave Luffy his famous straw hat,

00:03:27.269 --> 00:03:29.730
which inspired him to become a great pirate.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:35.280
And it’s a simple moment that I think a
lot of us take for granted, but without it

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.150
Luffy may never have gotten as far as he has
in the story.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:46.709
But we absolutely cannot talk about inspiration
without remembering this man’s epic finale.

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:52.080
Because in this climactic moment of Dr. Hiriluk’s
life, I was completely torn up inside.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:58.090
Young Chopper had mistakenly made a deadly
soup which was eaten by his only friend.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.750
I mean how terrible is that?

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:06.550
But instead of making Chopper guilty for killing
him, Hiriluk confronted the evil ruler of

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:11.050
their island and delivered the most epic speech
in the entire story.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:14.890
Then of course he did this.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:20.230
And wow, this was heartbreaking in so many
ways.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:24.521
For Chopper to lose the only person who really
cared about him, and for myself to see just

00:04:24.521 --> 00:04:27.800
how far this man would go to care for his
friend.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:33.539
*Sniff, and wipe eye.* Hey, I’m not crying,
that’s just a little water on the camera…

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:38.940
However, that moment isn’t even close to
the best moments that we’ll discuss later,

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:45.300
but first we have a scene that shows Luffy’s
incredible faith in his crew.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.300
When Sanji abandoned the crew to go to whole
cake island, Luffy said uh-uh, I’m not losing

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.300
my favorite cook.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:56.420
So he chased him down and finally caught up
to him right here.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:02.080
But Sanji genuinely thought he was doing what
was best for the crew and tried to trick Luffy

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:08.770
into leaving, even going so far as to beat
his captain like he was tenderizing a hunk

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:09.770
of meat.

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:14.040
And oh my god, this moment made me so mad
that Sanji would go this far.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:21.750
Yeah, Nami, hit him again!

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:28.389
But of course even after his beating, Luffy
continued to believe in Sanji and eventually

00:05:28.389 --> 00:05:29.860
brought him back to the crew.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:34.410
Which just goes to show just how much Luffy
loves his crew.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:38.970
Now, while that moment threatened to break
the bonds of the straw hat crew, this next

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:42.539
moment literally shook the world to its core.

00:05:42.539 --> 00:05:47.440
That’s because in Marineford we experienced
the heart-breaking loss of Luffy’s brother.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:54.889
And I never for a single moment thought we
would lose the world’s strongest man, Whitebeard,

00:05:54.889 --> 00:05:55.889
as well.

00:05:55.889 --> 00:06:00.520
But after tanking HUNDREDS of bullets, cannon
balls, sword attacks, and even having half

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:08.160
his face blown off, Whitebeard stood tall
and proclaimed that the One Piece is real.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:18.840
This moment made me shiver with its epicness,
and it reminded us that Luffy still had a

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.750
long way to go to reach his goals.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:27.460
But from that scene of pure sadness we shift
to what is maybe the greatest adrenaline rush

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:28.840
in the entire story.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:31.150
We’re in Sabaody.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:34.450
Luffy’s friend has just been shot by this
world noble.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:37.039
And Luffy is PISSED.

00:06:37.039 --> 00:06:44.280
He walks towards the celestial dragon, dodging
bullets, and absolutely smashes this guy into

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:45.900
the next dimension.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:52.640
And we HATED this guy, so it was so, so satisfying
to see him CRUSHED like that.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:57.650
But now before you go out and punch your most
hated enemy, make sure to subscribe to the

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.340
channel for more one piece content just like
this.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.470
But has your favorite moment shown up in the
ranking yet?

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:07.840
If not it might be just up ahead, because
this next moment, and character, is certainly

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:09.390
one I will never forget.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:17.890
And that’s because there is almost no character
we fell in love with faster than Corazon.

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:23.800
After just a few chapters I went from hating
him for kicking Law to loving him for taking

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.400
care of the sick and dying young doctor.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:32.520
But the moment I cried my eyes out was when
he let himself be killed just to give Law

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:33.800
a chance to live.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:39.810
And he even stayed alive long enough to hide
Law’s heartbreaking cries.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:44.940
And while this was one of the most impactful
deaths in the entire story, even it was not

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:49.470
as incredible as this moment right here.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:54.500
That’s because after Zoro was sliced up
like a cucumber, he holds up his sword and

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.740
shouts that he will NEVER.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:57.960
LOSE.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:59.180
AGAIN.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:02.389
And at the same time, he doubles down on his
loyalty to Luffy and the crew.

00:08:02.389 --> 00:08:04.020
Man, I love Zoro.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:09.270
But while that moment showed Zoro just how
far he has to go, this next moment showed

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:14.530
Luffy that he was nowhere near strong enough
to fulfill his dreams.

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:20.060
In Marineford after he struggled SO much to
save his brother, they could almost taste

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.060
freedom.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.620
Until this happened.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:29.449
And let me tell you, when I saw this for the
first time it was like I had my own massive

00:08:29.449 --> 00:08:30.720
hole in my chest.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:35.120
I was shocked and in physical pain.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:40.190
And as Luffy held his dying brother, it literally
broke his mind.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:41.769
And it broke me too.

00:08:41.769 --> 00:08:46.529
It just shows that the deeper the bonds of
brotherhood, the more heartbreaking it is

00:08:46.529 --> 00:08:51.680
when those bonds are broken.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.180
Which is exactly the same heartbreak I felt
during this next moment.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:09:00.820
That’s because when Luffy decided the crew
needed a new ship, his best friend, Usopp,

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.240
felt MASSIVELY betrayed.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:06.750
Usopp and the ship were so connected that
it felt like Luffy was choosing to get rid

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:12.329
of Usopp as well.And the argument got SO heated
that the two eventually had to square off

00:09:12.329 --> 00:09:13.330
in a duel.

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:16.590
And this was SO hard to watch.

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:22.890
Despite Usopp’s tricks, I knew all along
that he stood NO CHANCE of beating Luffy,

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.860
and our favorite sniper temporarily left the
crew.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:27.720
Gosh, this was tough.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:31.460
Kinda like having to say goodbye to a favorite
pet.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:35.860
Which is absolutely insane that this moment
didn’t make the top ten, but just wait until

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:41.870
you see the legendary, and actually surprising,
moments that are coming up at the end of this

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:42.870
video.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:45.959
Kicking it off with one of the coolest scenes
in the entire story.

00:09:45.959 --> 00:09:53.000
And if there is ever a moment that captures
the themes of the story it is this legendary

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.529
moment right here.

00:09:54.529 --> 00:09:57.020
People’s Dreams Don’t Ever End.

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:59.100
Which is true even in death.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:04.459
And there is one death in particular that
impacted ALL of the straw hats more than any

00:10:04.459 --> 00:10:05.459
other.

00:10:05.459 --> 00:10:06.459
Do you know which moment I’m talking about?

00:10:06.459 --> 00:10:09.740
It is of course the funeral of the Going Merry.

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:16.079
And boy did I NEVER EXPECT cry over a ship,
but that is exactly what happened when the

00:10:16.079 --> 00:10:19.790
crew put their first vessel to rest.

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:24.810
A true friend and crewmate was lost but never
forgotten.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:30.350
However, this moment was nowhere near as shocking
as this next one.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:34.980
And let me tell you that after all the death
and destruction that took place on the back

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:40.120
of this giant elephant, I never expected that
the animal minks were actually protecting

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:42.460
this samurai all this time.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:48.339
But when they said RAIZO IS SAFE, I literally
just had to sit and stare because my brain

00:10:48.339 --> 00:10:51.660
could not process what I was seeing.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:58.589
I mean, this cat and dog sacrificed an arm
and a leg, plus their whole country was almost

00:10:58.589 --> 00:10:59.589
wiped out.

00:10:59.589 --> 00:11:06.040
I truly thought that Raizo was not here, so
this moment hit me like almost no other one

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.040
in the story.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:12.230
And like I know friendship is kind of a meme
in anime, but there has never been a display

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:15.889
of loyalty more powerful than this one.

00:11:15.889 --> 00:11:22.959
Actually, let me take that back because this
next one is also god-tier levels of loyalty.

00:11:22.959 --> 00:11:29.480
That’s because this samurai survived an
ENTIRE HOUR in a ridiculously hot pot of boiling

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:39.139
oil WHILE literally carrying his entire crew
on his back To top it all off, Oden died with

00:11:39.139 --> 00:11:44.950
a smile showing us that this was truly a man
who gave everything of himself to protect

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.850
his friends, family, and country.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:53.180
And while Oden’s death was expected, I don’t
think anyone knew just how heroic his end

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.420
would be.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:59.649
But an even more unexpected twist came way
earlier in the story.

00:11:59.649 --> 00:12:04.490
In chapter 216, Vivi made the shocking choice
to NOT.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:05.490
JOIN.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.490
the.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:07.490
crew.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:11.260
And oh wow let me tell you there is not a
single character in the entire story that

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:15.880
the fanbase desperately wants to rejoin the
crew.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.730
People love Vivi.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:22.829
I mean she traveled with the straw hats for
so long, but in the end she left us a bit

00:12:22.829 --> 00:12:39.720
blue with this heart-felt speech and this
legendary scene where the crew show off their

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:40.720
X’s.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:45.230
*hold up your arm* Vivi for nakama.

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:49.639
Now, while Vivi chose to stay behind, when
another character finally joined the crew

00:12:49.639 --> 00:12:53.180
it made for one of the most emotional moments
in the story.

00:12:53.180 --> 00:13:00.830
And in my opinion it is the first truly gut-punching
scene in the entire story.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:05.990
For over seventy chapters, Nami was smart,
strong willed, and didn’t let anyone boss

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:06.990
her around.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:09.130
But that all changed in the Arlong Park arc.

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:13.080
In chapter 81 Nami had just lost EVERYTHING.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:17.399
Years of work to collect treasure to free
her village was stolen in an instant and she

00:13:17.399 --> 00:13:23.060
was powerless to free herself from these fishmen.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:28.360
So when she finally broke down and cried out
to Luffy for help, it made me want to suit

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:30.680
up and go fight Arlong myself.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:36.350
Whew, man, going through all of these moments
is like a roller coaster over here.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:41.430
But we still have the most impactful moments
still to come.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:48.160
At number four, is the moment that changed
the entire final saga of the story.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:56.709
This was Chapter 1044 in the manga - the awakening
of Gear 5 Luffy.

00:13:56.709 --> 00:14:05.449
And let me just say that this moment got my
heart pounding like almost no other.

00:14:05.449 --> 00:14:13.220
I had waited YEARS for Luffy’s Gear 5 transformation,
but I could never imagine that it would turn

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:15.660
out like this.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:19.529
And I LOVED IT.

00:14:19.529 --> 00:14:24.279
It was perfectly on brand for Luffy, and even
though I had SO MANY questions about his new

00:14:24.279 --> 00:14:30.000
powers, this moment combined some of the pre-time
skip wackiness with insanely cool new powers

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.509
for a truly epic moment in the story.

00:14:34.509 --> 00:14:40.000
Though even Gear 5 did not make me jump out
of my seat like this next one.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:44.480
And that’s because I have never been more
surprised at a single moment in One Piece

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:51.420
than when Charlotte Katakuri stabbed himself
during his fight with Luffy.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:57.140
And you may be surprised this moment is ranked
so high, but to me, it was just so completely

00:14:57.140 --> 00:15:06.460
unexpected that I will never forget the absolute
mind-boggling shock of this moment.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:10.519
Because after Luffy was tricked and nearly
knocked out by Katakuri’s sister, the mochi

00:15:10.519 --> 00:15:14.930
man could have easily finished the fight.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:21.019
Instead, he chose to even the playing field
by literally stabbing a hole through his stomach.

00:15:21.019 --> 00:15:28.470
No other villain in the story has EVER done
that, and it is one of the reasons Katakuri

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:31.529
is a fan favorite.

00:15:31.529 --> 00:15:36.350
And the number two most insanely impactful
moment is likely many people’s favorite

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:37.350
scene.

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:43.860
A moment of such excitement, relief, and pure
desperation when Robin finally told the crew:

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:45.610
I want to Live.

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:50.670
Even though Robin betrayed the crew and nearly
got them killed, they never gave up on her.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:57.560
They chased her across two islands, beat up
some secret agents, and even declared war

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:03.339
on the world government to show her that NOTHING
would stand in the way of saving her life.

00:16:03.339 --> 00:16:12.589
Which means that at number one is the most
legendary, epic, absolute pure moment of insane

00:16:12.589 --> 00:16:17.680
greatness in the story, which is Zoro’s
Nothing Happened.

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:19.779
And to be honest, what more do I need to say?

00:16:19.779 --> 00:16:24.380
Zoro is the peak of awesome and nothing surpasses
this moment for me.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:29.680
But this moment might have also been foreshadowing
for Zoro’s ultimate powerup later on in

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:30.680
the story.

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:35.590
Because an unbreakable will is what led him
to eventually unlock conquerors haki during

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:38.269
his fight with this god-like figure right
here.

00:16:38.269 --> 00:16:43.680
And this was such a legendary moment that
I had to include it in my ranking of the top

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:52.639
conquerors haki moments in the story, which
you can watch right here.

00:16:52.639 --> 00:16:54.700
Shanks for watching and I’ll see you in
the next one.

